# UI Slice 10's verification: three new painter primitives, on screen.
#
# The claim is that a chart became writable in a *consumer* — stroked polylines
# for the curves, filled convex polygons for the area under one of them, and a
# textured quad for a thumbnail the demo shaded itself — with no widget added to
# `slmsttaa-ui`, and with the overlay still a single `draw_indexed`. Three of
# those are pictures, and these are the pictures.
#
# Run it:  cargo xtask shoot terrain --script capture/terrain-plot.script
#
# Frame numbers, not seconds. The engine holds on each one, so a click lands on a
# known frame and the erosion is at a known pass — which is what makes the
# coordinates below stable rather than a guess about timing. At the default 8
# passes a second, frame N is pass N/7.5.
#
# Two things about the coordinates, both learned the hard way elsewhere:
#
#  - **They were read off `shot rest`**, in physical pixels from the window's
#    top-left. The pause button is at (97, 109); the Plot heading at (52, 227).
#  - **Every click here is on or above the Plot heading**, deliberately.
#    Collapsing a section reflows only the rows beneath it, so nothing in this
#    file moves under its own steps. That is the reflow trap
#    `capture/editor-list.script` records, sidestepped by ordering rather than
#    survived.
#
# **The pass is advanced by playing, not by scrubbing, and that is a harness
# limit rather than a preference.** The obvious script clicks four fifths of the
# way along the `pass` track and jumps straight to a drained landscape. It does
# nothing: `Action::Click` is a press *and* release with no update in between, so
# `Response::held` is never true for a single frame, and every drag widget in the
# toolkit — slider, and the demo's own `log_slider` — acts on `held`. A button
# works (the pause below is one), a slider cannot be moved at all. Recorded in
# the engine roadmap beside the wheel, which was added for the same class of
# reason: a widget the harness could not reach.

# Frame 200: about pass 26. Lakes full, both curves still climbing away from the
# origin, and the minimap wet. The reference shot, and where the coordinates
# above were read from.
200  shot  rest

# Frame 700: about pass 93, running. The curves have grown to the right and the
# marker with them; the area fill under lake depth has grown with both. Two
# shots of a plot that is being *made* is the cheapest proof the marker is a
# function of the pass rather than a decoration.
700  shot  mid

# Pause at about pass 136, so the last two shots hold still. The play/pause
# button is the left half of the Time section's two-column row, and a button is
# the one interactive thing a press-and-release can actually work.
1020  move  97 109
1040  click

# Frame 1080: the shot the whole section exists for. Lake depth has decayed to
# nearly nothing while height-moved has not, which is the demo's own headless
# measurement — "lake coverage falls to zero by about pass 110", written in
# `terrain.rs` since Slice 14 and never once on screen — finally drawn. The
# minimap has lost its water at the same time, from the same data, which is what
# says the image and the plot are two views of one thing rather than two
# pictures that happen to agree.
1080  shot  late

# Collapse the Plot heading. Everything below it moves up and the panel shrinks,
# which proves the section is an ordinary `ui.section` with no privileges — and
# leaves a picture of the demo with the capability switched off to diff against.
1120  move  52 227
1140  click
1180  shot  collapsed
